<?php
/*
==========================================================================
 NOTES: Webmail one-click login (Roundcube)  --  not executable code
==========================================================================

Q: If I change RoundcubeAutoLogin('https://www.german-emirates-club.com/admin/_webmail/')
   to 'https://buenapublica.cmpsrv.com/rc/', does it work?

A: No. The script logs in from our server, so the login cookies end up on
   german-emirates-club.com. A browser can't use cookies from one domain on
   another, so when it is redirected to buenapublica.cmpsrv.com/rc/ it has no
   session there and Roundcube shows the login form. One-click login into /rc/
   needs something running on buenapublica.cmpsrv.com (an SSO plugin or a
   script there), which only the hosting provider can add.

What will work: keep the URL as https://www.german-emirates-club.com/admin/_webmail/
and fix the script. It's our own Roundcube (1.4.13) on the same server, so it
reads the same mailboxes as /rc/ (config: default_host = 'localhost').

Likely bug: the server answers with HTTP/1.1, so Apache sends the cookie header
as "Set-Cookie:" with capitals. __class_roundcube.php searches only for
lowercase "set-cookie:", so it finds no cookies and the user lands on the
login form.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
 STEP 1 - Back up (OUTSIDE the web root, so .bak files can't be downloaded)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
    mkdir -p ~/backups
    cd ~/buenapublica/german-emirates-club.com/admin
    cp classes/__class_roundcube.php ~/backups/__class_roundcube.php.bak
    cp webmail-login.php ~/backups/webmail-login.php.bak

 To undo: copy those two files back to their original places.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
 STEP 2 - admin/classes/__class_roundcube.php, in login()
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Replace:

    preg_match_all('/set-cookie: (.*)\b/', $response, $cookies);
    $cookie_return = array();
    foreach($cookies[1] as $cookie)
    {
        preg_match('|([A-z0-9\_]*)=([A-z0-9\_\-]*);|', $cookie, $cookie_match);
        if($cookie_match) {
            $cookie_return[$cookie_match[1]] = $cookie_match[2];
        }
    }
    return $cookie_return;

 With:

    preg_match_all('/^set-cookie:\s*([^=;\s]+)=([^;\r\n]*)/mi', $response, $m, PREG_SET_ORDER);
    $cookie_return = array();
    foreach ($m as $c) {
        if ($c[2] !== '' && $c[2] !== 'deleted') {   // skip cookies Roundcube is clearing
            $cookie_return[$c[1]] = $c[2];           // last value wins
        }
    }
    return $cookie_return;

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
 STEP 3 - admin/classes/__class_roundcube.php, in redirect()
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
 The parameter needs the underscore, and the script should stop afterwards:

    header('Location: ' . $this->_rc_link . '?_task=mail');
    exit;

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
 STEP 4 - admin/webmail-login.php
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Stop the foreach from running on null when the login fails:

    $cookies = $rc->login($_POST['_user'], $_POST['_pass']) ?: array();

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
 STEP 5 - Test
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
 - No service restart needed: PHP reads the files on every request.
   If OPcache shows old behaviour, wait about a minute and retry.
 - Test in a private/incognito window, or clear the cookies for
   german-emirates-club.com first.
 - Still showing the login form? Ask for a debug version that prints
   exactly what Roundcube sends back.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Other checks
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Encryption-key check (use single quotes; bash treats ! specially in double quotes).
 Run inside ~/buenapublica/german-emirates-club.com/admin/_webmail:

    grep -cF 'rcmail-!24ByteDESkey*Str' config/config.inc.php

 1 = default des_key still in use -> set a random 24-character string.
 0 = already changed.
*/
